# Third-party data and software

## Encyclopedia of Polyhedra (George W. Hart)

`src/data/polyhedra.json` contains vertex and face data for the Platonic,
Archimedean and Johnson solids derived from the mathematical model files of the
Encyclopedia of Polyhedra by George W. Hart (https://www.georgehart.com/).

Hart's copyright notice states that, while the text and images of Virtual
Polyhedra are all-rights-reserved, the individual model files are different:

> An exception is the collection of individual *.wrl files which contain the
> mathematical description of each polyhedron. Because these contain
> mathematical information, they may be of use to others with an interest in
> polyhedra. They may be reproduced and used for noncommercial purposes.

This project is non-commercial and distributes that data on those terms. The
data was re-exported via the `polyhedra` npm package
(https://github.com/finnp/polyhedra); see `scripts/generate-catalog.ts`.

Every other model in the catalog — Kepler-Poinsot solids, Catalan duals,
prisms, antiprisms, bipyramids, trapezohedra, pyramids, cupolae, compounds and
geodesic spheres — is generated from first principles by this project's own
code and carries no third-party terms.

## Category structure

The catalog hierarchy follows the one used by Stella 4D / Great Stella
(https://www.software3d.com/), which is an excellent piece of software and
worth buying. No Stella code or data is used here.

